* =====================================================================================================
* sleep_current__w25q128jv.lib -- W25Q128JV QSPI NOR flash in deep power-down, DC model
*
* Part      : Winbond W25Q128JVSIQ (main board U11, VCC = +3V3, /CS pulled up by R10 and the nRF CSN pull-up)
* Datasheet : https://www.winbond.com/resource-files/w25q128jv%20revf%2003272018%20plus.pdf
*             (W25Q128JV Revision F, March 27, 2018)
*
* Modelled (§9.4 DC Electrical Characteristics):
*   ICC2  power-down current 1 uA typ / 20 uA max, /CS = VCC, VIN = GND or VCC
*   ILI   input leakage +-2 uA max: max corner only, as a sink on /CS (the only flash input held at a rail;
*         SCK and IO0-IO3 float in sleep because the nRF QSPI sleep pinctrl disconnects them).
*   MAXC = 0 typical, 1 datasheet maximum.
*
* Supply currents are scaled by tanh(V/50 mV) so that they vanish on an unpowered rail (ship mode).
* NOT modelled: the floating SCK / IO0-IO3 inputs. ICC2 is specified with every input at GND or VCC; a floating
*   CMOS input can draw extra through-current, which a DC model cannot predict. Standby ICC1 (10 / 60 uA)
*   applies if deep power-down is not entered (firmware §12.5 requires it).
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt SC_W25Q128JV_PD vcc csn vss params: MAXC=0
.param icc2 = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 20u : 1u}
.param ili  = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 2u : 0}
Bcc vcc vss I = 'icc2 * tanh(v(vcc,vss)/0.05)'
Bcs csn vss I = 'ili * tanh(v(csn,vss)/0.1)'
.ends SC_W25Q128JV_PD
